node_modules/
dist/
# bench/results/*.json IS tracked — every number in README.md and the design spec
# has to resolve to a file someone who clones this can open. What is not tracked is
# the verbatim report text those runs produced: it embeds ~1 MB of source from the
# benchmark corpus, which is a private third-party repository.
#
# That separation is enforced by `bench/run.ts`, not by hand. The sweep writes the
# untouched reports HERE first, then strips them from the artifact it writes to
# bench/results/ and scans the serialised result for leaked report text before
# writing it; a leak aborts the write rather than producing a file that looks
# committable. `npm run bench -- --verify-artifacts` re-checks every file already
# in bench/results/ and is worth running before any `git add` of that directory.
#
# This line is the last defence, not the first. Do not remove it, and do not force
# anything under it into a commit.
bench/results/raw-reports/
*.log
.claude-flow/
